EXECUTIVE SUMMARY

This document transfers the ROBUC model to academic research partners for 
rigorous validation before any legislative pitch. The model is a universal 
care financing and delivery system that uses reverse Vickrey auctions to align 
Advocates (integrated care providers) with outcome-based incentives. This memo 
specifies the mechanism, validation strategy, critical unknowns, and decision 
framework.

Next Step: Academic partners undertake agent-based modeling (ABM) and 
international benchmarking studies to establish feasibility before we approach 
a legislator for a pilot investment (~$50 million, ~5K underserved residents, 
~7-8 regions).

================================================================================
SECTION 1: MECHANISM SUMMARY
================================================================================

1.1 REGIONAL STRUCTURE

Each region contains 20,000 people and is served by a single winning Advocate 
(e.g., clinic network, ACO, hospital-affiliated group, or boutique community 
provider).

1.2 THE REVERSE VICKREY AUCTION

Advocates submit sealed bids in two parts:

  Bid Value = Fixed Rate + Expectation Value of Bonus (roughly half)

Where:
  - Fixed Rate: Annual per-capita payment the Advocate receives regardless 
    of outcomes.
  - Expectation Value of Bonus: Bonuses awarded based on health rankings. 
Expectation value is the sum of all bonus tiers divided by the number of 
bonus tiers which is likely around half of the maximum bonus.

Winning Rule: Lowest total bid wins.

Payment Rule: The winner receives their own fixed rate. The 
bonus amount expands to match the second-lowest bid's total value.

Rationale: Advocates bid their true willingness-to-accept (dominant strategy 
in a second-price auction). The mechanism filters for efficiency: lower-cost, 
higher-confidence providers win.

1.3 TENURE AND RE-BIDDING

  - Year 1: Fixed rate only; bonus determined at end of 12-month performance 
    window (performance metrics may need to be calculated early at first).
  - Year 2+: For healthy regions (in top 4/5 of composite health metric), 
    fixed rate and bonus are inflation-adjusted and continued without re-bidding. For 
    unhealthy regions, re-bid conducted annually. 
  - Patient Transfer: Incoming Advocate automatically assumes all patients; 
    no patient opt-out; outgoing Advocate delivers final month of service; 
    payment tendered upon complete patient handoff certification.

1.4 ANTI-MONOPOLY CONSTRAINT

No Advocate may hold contracts for more than 1/10 of all regions nationwide.

1.5 PENALTY SYSTEM

  1. Regional Underperformance: Regions ranking in the bottom 1/5 (by composite 
     metric) are lost. The Advocate cannot re-bid for that specific region in 
     the next cycle.
  2. Systemic Incompetence: If an Advocate's cumulative loss rate (regions lost 
     ÷ regions held) exceeds 1/5, that Advocate is barred from bidding across 
     all regions for the following 12 months.
  3. Boutique advocates (who hold less than 3 regions and are founded by members 
     of the served community (residence and background) may apply for a three 
     year exemption from rebid to enhance continuity of care. 

