SECTION 2: EQUITY GUARDRAILS
================================================================================

2.1 BOUTIQUE ADVOCATES & SBA SUPPORT

The Small Business Administration funds and trains BOUTIQUE ADVOCATES—community-
owned or -operated providers in poorly served regions. Boutique curricula 
include:

  - Procurement of telehealth services to mitigate geographic access barriers.
  - Coordination with community health workers (CHWs) and local clinics.
  - Financial training (risk management, bonding, baseline operational costs).
  - Actuarial guidance to identify effective caregivers

Outcome: Boutique Advocates can undercut incumbent bids in underserved markets 
and build permanent infrastructure (gyms, clinics, grocery partnerships).

2.2.A METRICS

Government chooses metrics and metric weights by three criteria: availability,
economic impact and population health. Before medical data pipline is built, 
metrics rely on existing government data such as mortality rates by age, 
disability rates by age, unemployment, etc... Initial statistics must also 
prioritize slow changes in medical sector size and shape to blunt shock of 
wholesale economic change. While initial statistics may not as closely mirror
population health, data pipeline maturity enables better and more impactful
metrics.

2.2.B DISPARITY METRICS

Government establishes a RACE-NEUTRAL STATUTE with explicit demographic 
tracking for:

  - Maternal mortality/morbidity
  - Female acute myocardial infarction outcomes
  - Diabetes control
  - Opioid overdose/treatment
  - Colorectal/breast/prostate cancer screening and mortality
  - Hypertension control
  - Kidney disease progression
  - Mental health and suicide prevention

Each metric contributes to the composite health score.

2.3 METRIC GOVERNANCE

  - Government sets bonus metrics unilaterally (with input from bureaucrats, 
    politicians, and external advisors).
  - All metrics must be public >= 6 months before implementation.
  - Metrics are composite (not causally attributed) and will change to prevent 
    Goodharting.

