SECTION 6: ENTITIES AND ROLES
================================================================================

6.1 GOVERNMENT

  - Collects taxes and allocates budget to regions.
  - Pays fixed rates and bonuses to winning Advocates.
  - Provides baseline health/cost metrics and validates regional performance.
  - Sets bonus metrics unilaterally; metrics must be public >= 6 months before 
    implementation.
  - Oversees Auction House licensing and anti-monopoly enforcement.
  - Oversees region map and adjustments with population changes.

6.2 AUCTION HOUSES (Profit & Non-Profit)

National data marketplaces competing on fee structures, data packaging, and 
brand reputation. Roles:

  - Hold sealed bids during auction.
  - Provide patient record access (sandboxed) to blinded researchers.
  - Bundle research requests to preserve buyer anonymity and prevent corruption.
  - Auction research tasks to researchers.
  - Assign and validate researchers via billing codes, interviews, registries.
  - Sell population health models, statistics, and benchmarking data to 
    Advocates.
  - Propose mid-year metric adjustments (subject to government approval).

6.3 ADVOCATES

  - Deliver or coordinate care for assigned patients.
  - Submit sealed bids (fixed rate + expectation value of bonus).
  - Manage copays and out-of-pocket patient costs.
  - Assume all patients from outgoing Advocate upon winning bid.
  - No secondary mid-year region transfers.
  - Subject to anti-monopoly (max 1/10 of all regions) and penalty rules.

6.4 RESEARCHERS

  - Blinded to Advocate/buyer identity.
  - Bid on research projects via Auction Houses.
  - Assigned by Auction Houses and validated through billing codes, interviews, 
    and registries.
  - Access sandboxed patient records.
  - Contribute to outcome metrics and health surveillance.

6.5 PATIENTS

  - Automatically transfer to new Advocate upon regional re-bid.
  - No opt-out on Advocate transfer.
  - Freedom to seek external care at own expense.
  - Access sandboxed own records via Auction Houses.
  - Served by Advocate for preventive, acute, and chronic care.

6.6 SBA (SMALL BUSINESS ADMINISTRATION)

  - Active role in fostering boutique Advocates in poorly served regions.
  - Provides training curriculum, startup capital, and ongoing support.
  - Supports telemedicine procurement and CHW integration.
  - Tracks boutique market share and outcomes vs. incumbent Advocates.

