APPENDIX A: GLOSSARY

Advocate: An integrated care provider (clinic, ACO, hospital network, or 
boutique health organization) that bids to serve a region and manages all care 
for enrolled patients under capitated payment + outcome bonuses.

Auction House: A national data marketplace that holds sealed bids, provides 
patient record access to blinded researchers, and sells population health data 
products to Advocates.

Bonus Metric: A composite health outcome score determined by government, used to 
calculate year-end bonus payments to the winning Advocate.

Boutique Advocate: A community-owned or -operated care provider in an underserved 
region, supported by the SBA through training, capital, and mentorship.

Capitated Payment: Per-capita, fixed annual payment to an Advocate (independent 
of utilization).

Composite Score: Single health outcome metric combining primary metrics (life 
expectancy, mortality, etc.) and disparity metrics (maternal mortality, diabetes 
control, etc.).
